  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Girls Not Brides 2020 - 2025 - Girls Not Brides 2020 - 2022 (New strategy 2018-2022)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Girls Not Brides 2020 - 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Girls Not Brides (GNB): Global Partnership to End Child Marriage, &#xe4;r ett globalt partnerskap med mer &#xe4;n 1 350 civilsamh&#xe4;llsorganisationer fr&#xe5;n 100 l&#xe4;nder som arbetar mot barn&#xe4;ktenskap. Sidas k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d p&#xe5; 40 MSEK kommer att st&#xf6;dja GNB:s k&#xe4;rnverksamhet f&#xf6;r perioden 2020&#x2013;2023. GNB:s totala budget &#xe4;r 282 MSEK.

GNB spelar en viktig roll inom r&#xf6;relsen mot barn&#xe4;ktenskap genom att mobilisera kollektiva &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder och st&#xf6;d p&#xe5; nationell, regional och internationell niv&#xe5; samt st&#xf6;d &#xe5;t medlemsorganisationer f&#xf6;r att bygga upp sin kapacitet, f&#xf6;respr&#xe5;kande f&#xf6;r ekonomiska resurser och sprida l&#xe4;rande och kunskap om barn&#xe4;ktenskap. Genom detta arbete skapar GNB en plattform f&#xf6;r att mobilisera arbetet mot barn&#xe4;ktenskap.

Partnerskapet grundades 2011 och st&#xf6;ds av ett sekretariat i London med regional personal i New Delhi, Mexico City, Nairobi och Dakar med totalt 35 anst&#xe4;llda. GNB arbetar fr&#xe4;mst genom sitt globala n&#xe4;tverk och medlemmar. GNB:s diversifierade n&#xe4;tverk f&#xf6;renar organisationer som arbetar mot barn&#xe4;ktenskap utifr&#xe5;n ett antal perspektiv som utbildning, h&#xe4;lsa och r&#xe4;ttsstatsprincipen. Cirka 80% av GNB:s medlemmar arbetar p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5;, medan mindre &#xe4;n 10% av GNB:s medlemmar &#xe4;r internationella icke-statliga organisationer.

Syftet med insatsen &#xe4;r att st&#xf6;dja GNB:s k&#xe4;rnarbete i linje med sekretariatsstrategin f&#xf6;r 2019&#x2013;2023, som styrs av sex m&#xe5;l: 1) Effektiva kollektiva &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder i det civila samh&#xe4;llet p&#xe5; alla niv&#xe5;er; 2) R&#xf6;relsen har bevis, information och l&#xe4;rande f&#xf6;r att vidta effektiva &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder: 3) En m&#xe5;ngfaldig r&#xf6;relse med att g&#xf6;ra sina r&#xf6;ster h&#xf6;rda p&#xe5; alla niv&#xe5;er och skapa en plattform f&#xf6;r samh&#xe4;llsbaserade organisationer, kvinnor, flickor och ungdomar; 4) Sekretariatet Girls Not Brides &#xe4;r funktionellt, effektivt och kan st&#xf6;dja r&#xf6;relsen mot barn&#xe4;ktenskap; 5) Regeringar och andra beslutsfattare vidtar effektiva &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder; och 6) R&#xf6;relsen som arbetar mot barn&#xe4;ktenskapet har tillr&#xe4;ckliga resurser.

Som en del av sekretariatsstrategin 2019&#x2013;2023 kommer GNB att fokusera p&#xe5; att st&#xe4;rka strategiskt st&#xf6;d till medlemmar i ett antal prioriterade l&#xe4;nder, st&#xe4;rka sitt arbete med k&#xf6;nstransformativa tillv&#xe4;gag&#xe5;ngss&#xe4;tt, arbeta med flickors r&#xe4;ttigheter i humanit&#xe4;ra milj&#xf6;er samt st&#xe4;rka ungdomsengagemang och ledarskap.

Insatsen f&#xf6;r 2020&#x2013;2023 bygger p&#xe5; det v&#xe4;l etablerade samarbetet mellan GNB och Sida under 2017&#x2013;2019, d&#xe4;r Sida gav k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d till GNB.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Girls Not Brides (GNB): The Global Partnership to End Child Marriage, is a global partnership of more than 1,350 civil society organisations from 100 countries working to address and end child marriage. Core support of 40 MSEK will be provided to GNB for the period 2020-2023. GNB&apos;s total budget is 282 MSEK. 

GNB plays a important role within the movement to end child marriage by mobilising collective action and support at the national, regional, and international levels, supporting member organisations to build their capacity, advocating for financial resources, and facilitating learning and knowledge Exchange on ending child marriage. Through this work, GNB creates a platform for mobilising efforts to end child marriage.

GNB was established in 2011 and is supported by a Secretariat in London and regional staff in New Delhi, Mexico City, Nairobi and Dakar, with a total of 35 staff. GNB&apos;s works mainly through its global network and members. GNB&#x2019;s diverse network unites organisations approaching the issue of child marriage from a range of perspectives such as education, health and rule of law. Around 80% of GNB&#x2019;s members work at the community level, while less than 10% of GNB&#x2019;s members are international NGOs.

The purpose of the intervention is to support GNB&apos;s core work as described in their 2019-2023 Secretariat Strategy which is guided by six objectives: 1) Effective civil society collective action at all levels; 2) The movement has evidence, information and learning to take effective action: 3) A diverse movement exists with voices amplified at all levels and providing a platform for community-based organisations, women, girls and youth; 4) The Girls Not Brides Secretariat is functional, effective and able to support the movement to end child marriage; 5) Governments and other decision-makers take effective action; and 6) The movement to end child marriage has sufficient resources.

As part of the 2019-2023 Secretariat strategy, GNB will focus on strengthening strategic support to members in a number of prioritised countries,  strengthening its work on gender transformative approaches, addressing girls&#x2019; rights in humanitarian contexts and settings, and strengthen youth engagement and leadership. 

The intervention for 2020-2023 is builds upon the well established cooperation between GNB and Sida from 2017-2019, in which Sida supported GNB with core support.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The vision for GnB is a world without child marriage where girls and women enjoy equal status with boys and men and are able to achieve their full potential in all aspects of their lives.

The intervention is aligned with Girls not Brides (GnB) Partnership Strategy as well as GNBs Secretariat Strategy, both for 2002-2025. The strategies build on previous strategies (2017-2020).

The Partnership Strategy identifies a set of six shared goals which aim to focus the work as a Partnership and maximise impact for the four year period 2022-2025. The goals are geared towards:

A) communities as the drivers of change, with girls and women at the centre;

B) governments leading effective action and fostering civil society participation;

C) the global community championing and supporting initiatives to end child marriage;

D) more sustainable, long-term funding available, particularly for communities;

E) evidence and learning  is the basis for work to address child marriage;

F) collective engagement through a diverse global Partnership is at the core.

The Secretariat Strategy has four objectives which will guide GNB&apos;s work during the 2022-2025 period:

1) Movement-building. Leverage the collective power of the global Partnership of member organisations, National and State Partnerships and coalitions for accelerated action to end child marriage.

2) Influencing. Galvanise the wider global end child marriage movement to drive change nationally, regionally and globally.

3) Learning. Leverage knowledge, learning and evidence to address child  marriage across themovement.

4) Secretariat at the service of the global Partnership. Continue to develop as a sustainable and values-based organisation at the service of the global Partnership.</narrative>
  </description>
